{#
compose/_to_row.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The To row, and directly under it the refusal that belongs to it.

Rendered in ONE of two places, never both, and which one depends on where the
window lives:

  • `compact: true`  — in an inline window's HEADER, where the recipient
    summary used to be. That summary was a button reading "to Someone" (or
    "No recipients") that unfolded the whole address block, and on a forward —
    which opens with no recipient at all and needs exactly one thing typed
    into it — it was a label standing in front of the only field that
    mattered. It IS the field now: same widget, same target, same everything
    below, just laid out for a header row. The chevron beside it still unfolds
    From/Cc/Bcc/Subject for the rarer case.

  • `compact: false` — first in the address block of a dock window, where it
    has always been.

One partial rather than two markups because everything that reads this row
addresses it by target — the Tom Select taming, the panel-room reservation,
the tab order, the aria wiring, the invalid marking — and a second copy is a
second thing for those to drift out of step with.

The <label for> is load-bearing, not decoration: Tom Select hides the <select>
and builds its own text input, and copies the accessible name across only when
a label is bound to the select's id. The controller mirrors it onto the
generated input as well, belt with braces.

Variables: form, compact (default false)
#}
{% set compact = compact|default(false) %}

<div class="{{ compact ? 'min-w-0 flex-1' : 'shrink-0' }}">
    <div data-compose--compose-target="toField"
         {# The suggestion panel OVERLAYS from here rather than pushing the
            window about. In the dock the panel is given real room — it hangs
            over the Subject row otherwise, and a click aimed at Subject
            commits a contact nobody chose (see
            compose--compose#_reserveRoomForPanel). Here there is no Subject
            below to cover: the row is the header, and reserving room for the
            panel grew the header and shoved the whole editor down every time
            a result arrived. This attribute is what tells the controller which
            of the two rows it is looking at. #}
         {% if compact %}data-compose-overlay-panel{% endif %}
         {# `select-text`: the inline header carries `select-none` so the
            window chrome cannot be dragged into a text selection, and it is
            inherited — which in a header that now contains a typing surface
            would fight the caret. #}
         class="flex items-center gap-3 min-h-[36px] select-text
                {{ compact ? '' : 'px-4 py-1.5' }}">
        <label for="{{ form.toAddresses.vars.id }}"
               id="{{ form.toAddresses.vars.id }}_label"
               class="text-xs font-medium text-ink-faint shrink-0
                      {{ compact ? '' : 'w-10 text-right' }}">{{ 'compose.to'|trans }}</label>
        <div class="flex-1 min-w-0">
            {{ form_widget(form.toAddresses) }}
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-2 shrink-0">
            <button type="button"
                    data-compose--compose-target="ccBtn"
                    data-action="click->compose--compose#showCc"
                    {# title, not aria-label: the button already has an
                       accessible name — the word "Cc" on its face — and
                       an aria-label would replace it rather than add to
                       it, leaving the visible label and the spoken one
                       saying different things (WCAG 2.5.3). #}
                    title="{{ 'compose.add_cc'|trans }}"
                    class="text-xs text-ink-faint hover:text-accent transition-colors">
                {{ 'compose.cc'|trans }}
            </button>
            <button type="button"
                    data-compose--compose-target="bccBtn"
                    data-action="click->compose--compose#showBcc"
                    title="{{ 'compose.add_bcc'|trans }}"
                    class="text-xs text-ink-faint hover:text-accent transition-colors">
                {{ 'compose.bcc'|trans }}
            </button>
        </div>
    </div>

    {# Why a send was refused. Rendered from the form rather than from a
       toast so it sits with the field it is about, and so a refusal
       that came from the server reads the same as one the window
       caught itself. It travels WITH the row: in a compact header the
       address block below is folded away, and a refusal nobody can see is
       the oldest bug in this window. #}
    <div data-compose--compose-target="errors"
         class="{{ compact ? '' : 'px-4' }} {{ form.toAddresses.vars.errors|length > 0 ? 'py-1' : 'hidden' }}"
         role="alert" aria-live="polite">
        <p class="text-xs text-danger">
            {%- for error in form.toAddresses.vars.errors %}{{ error.message }}{% endfor -%}
        </p>
    </div>
</div>
